<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms FormNumeric.Designer.cs — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgIO — on-screen numeric keypad entry dialog (Avalonia view).

    1:1 visual-parity reimplementation of the deleted WinForms `Forms/FormNumeric`
    (FormNumeric.cs + FormNumeric.Designer.cs). Per AAP §0.3.3 this is parity to the currently
    rendered Windows Forms UI — never a redesign (no new colors, no relayout, no UX changes).
    The dialog presents the current value in a large read-only display, the allowed minimum and
    maximum beneath it, a pair of up/down nudge buttons, the shared on-screen NumKeypad for entry,
    and explicit OK / Cancel command buttons.

    DATA BINDING (MVVM, compiled bindings via x:DataType="vm:FormNumericViewModel"):
      * tboxNumber.Text  -> EntryText  : the running typed string the keypad edits (read-only display).
      * lblMin.Text      -> Min        : the inclusive minimum guard (WinForms lblMin).
      * lblMax.Text      -> Max        : the inclusive maximum guard (WinForms lblMax).
    FormNumericViewModel owns the editing rules (AppendKey), the nudges (Increment/Decrement) and
    validation (TryGetResult); it owns NO OK/Cancel result state — the dialog outcome is produced by
    the hosting Window's code-behind (Close(value) / Close(null)), mirroring the WinForms
    DialogResult.OK / DialogResult.Cancel contract.

    WIRING CONTRACT — the partner code-behind (FormNumeric.axaml.cs) owns ALL behaviour, NOT this markup:
      * This view declares NO Click="..." handlers and NO event attributes. Every interactive control
        is addressed purely by x:Name so the code-behind subscribes/handles via the generated x:Name
        fields, with zero compile-time coupling to handler method names. The x:Names MUST stay exactly
        keypad1, btnOK, btnCancel, btnDistanceUp, btnDistanceDn, tboxNumber, lblMin, lblMax.
      * keypad1.ButtonPressed (the Keypad.GenericKeypad event, carrying e.KeyChar) is subscribed in the
        code-behind, reproducing the WinForms RegisterKeypad1_ButtonPressed routing: 'K' (OK) validates
        against Min/Max and closes with the value; 'X' (Cancel) closes with no value; every other token
        (digits, '.', '-', 'C', 'B') is forwarded to FormNumericViewModel.AppendKey.
      * btnOK / btnCancel reproduce the same OK / Cancel outcomes as explicit, touch-friendly buttons
        (the NumKeypad additionally carries its own 'K'/'X' keys; both paths converge on the same logic).
      * btnDistanceUp / btnDistanceDn reproduce the WinForms BtnDistanceUp_MouseDown /
        BtnDistanceDn_MouseDown single-step nudges -> FormNumericViewModel.Increment / Decrement.

    WINDOW SHELL — mirrors FormNumeric.Designer.cs (+ FormNumeric.cs ctor which set Text "Enter Value"):
      Text "Enter Value"                       -> Title (the ctor overrode the designer's "Enter a Value").
      BackColor SystemColors.ActiveCaption      -> Background "#99B4D1" (theme-independent parity color;
                                                   AgIO is light-only per App.axaml — no day/night).
      ShowInTaskbar = false                     -> ShowInTaskbar="False".
      TopMost (modal-over-owner)                -> Topmost="True" (consistent with sibling AgIO dialogs).
      StartPosition.CenterParent                -> WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner".
      FixedDialog (non-resizable)               -> CanResize="False" + SizeToContent="WidthAndHeight".
      Font Tahoma (base)                        -> FontFamily="Tahoma" (children set explicit sizes below).

    ASSETS: AgIO registers NO btnImages as <AvaloniaResource>, so avares://AgIO/... imagery would not
    resolve; per the established AgIO convention every command affordance is rendered as text (no
    System.Drawing, no WinForms, no avares images). WinForms points -> Avalonia DIP (x 96/72 ≈ x1.333):
    27.75pt -> 37; 14.25pt -> 19.
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        xmlns:vm="clr-namespace:AgIO.Views"
        xmlns:keypad="clr-namespace:Keypad;assembly=Keypad"
        x:Class="AgIO.Views.FormNumeric"
        x:DataType="vm:FormNumericViewModel"
        Title="Enter Value"
        SizeToContent="WidthAndHeight"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        CanResize="False"
        Topmost="True"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        SystemDecorations="Full"
        FontFamily="Tahoma"
        Background="#99B4D1">

    <!-- Fixed 456-wide content (matches the NumKeypad's intrinsic 456 px width) so SizeToContent
         yields a deterministic window width; the three Auto rows stack the top bar, the keypad, and
         the OK/Cancel command row, and SizeToContent computes the height. -->
    <Grid Width="456" RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto,Auto">

        <!--
            TOP BAR (WinForms y 0..112): the nudge buttons sit to the LEFT of the value display, with
            the min/max guard labels beneath it — reproducing the FormNumeric.Designer.cs arrangement
            (btnDistanceDn @x4, btnDistanceUp @x112, tboxNumber @x208, lblMin @x205, lblMax @x332).
        -->
        <Grid Grid.Row="0" ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" Margin="6,8,6,4">

            <!--
                btnDistanceDn / btnDistanceUp — WinForms AgLibrary.Controls.RepeatButton nudges, each
                91x92, wired to MouseDown (a single step per press). Reproduced as plain Buttons (one
                step per click, matching the WinForms single-fire MouseDown) whose Click is wired in the
                code-behind to FormNumericViewModel.Decrement / Increment. Down is LEFT, Up is RIGHT,
                matching the designer's x4 / x112 ordering. Text glyphs (no avares imagery on AgIO).
            -->
            <StackPanel Grid.Column="0"
                        Orientation="Horizontal"
                        Spacing="6"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center">
                <Button x:Name="btnDistanceDn"
                        Content="&#x25BC;"
                        Width="88" Height="88"
                        FontSize="28"
                        HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                        VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                        ToolTip.Tip="Decrease by 1" />
                <Button x:Name="btnDistanceUp"
                        Content="&#x25B2;"
                        Width="88" Height="88"
                        FontSize="28"
                        HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                        VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                        ToolTip.Tip="Increase by 1" />
            </StackPanel>

            <!-- Value display + guard labels (fill the remaining width, ≈ WinForms 246-wide column). -->
            <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Margin="8,0,0,0" VerticalAlignment="Center">

                <!--
                    tboxNumber — WinForms TextBox: Tahoma 27.75pt Bold, 246x52, ReadOnly, TextAlign
                    Center. Read-only because every edit flows through the on-screen keypad (and the
                    nudges), never physical keyboard focus. The designer's design-time placeholder is
                    intentionally dropped; the value is supplied at runtime via the bound EntryText.
                -->
                <TextBox x:Name="tboxNumber"
                         Height="52"
                         FontSize="37" FontWeight="Bold"
                         IsReadOnly="True"
                         TextAlignment="Center"
                         VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                         Text="{Binding EntryText}" />

                <!--
                    lblMin (LEFT) / lblMax (RIGHT) — WinForms Labels: Tahoma 14.25pt Bold, TopCenter,
                    showing the inclusive allowed range. Bound to the view-model's Min / Max. Named so
                    the code-behind can recolor them (the WinForms 'K' handler reddened the violated
                    bound on an out-of-range entry).
                -->
                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,*" Margin="0,4,0,0">
                    <TextBlock x:Name="lblMin"
                               Grid.Column="0"
                               FontSize="19" FontWeight="Bold"
                               TextAlignment="Center"
                               Text="{Binding Min}" />
                    <TextBlock x:Name="lblMax"
                               Grid.Column="1"
                               FontSize="19" FontWeight="Bold"
                               TextAlignment="Center"
                               Text="{Binding Max}" />
                </Grid>
            </StackPanel>
        </Grid>

        <!--
            keypad1 — the migrated Avalonia Keypad.NumKeypad UserControl (4x4 on-screen numeric keypad).
            WinForms: BackColor ActiveCaption, Location (0,112), Size 454x429. Its ButtonPressed event is
            subscribed in the code-behind (not declared here). Background matches the dialog's parity
            color so the inter-button gutters blend seamlessly with the window.
        -->
        <keypad:NumKeypad x:Name="keypad1"
                          Grid.Row="1"
                          Width="456" Height="430"
                          HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                          Background="#99B4D1" />

        <!--
            OK / Cancel command row. Cancel precedes OK so OK stays right-aligned (the conventional
            accept-on-the-right placement, consistent with the sibling FormYes dialog). btnCancel ->
            close with no value (DialogResult.Cancel); btnOK (IsDefault, so Enter confirms) -> validate
            and close with the value (DialogResult.OK). Both are wired in the code-behind. Touch-friendly
            sizing; text content (no avares imagery on AgIO).
        -->
        <StackPanel Grid.Row="2"
                    Orientation="Horizontal"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                    Spacing="12"
                    Margin="6,6,6,8">
            <Button x:Name="btnCancel"
                    Content="Cancel"
                    Width="120" Height="60"
                    FontSize="18"
                    HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                    VerticalContentAlignment="Center" />
            <Button x:Name="btnOK"
                    Content="OK"
                    IsDefault="True"
                    Width="120" Height="60"
                    FontSize="18"
                    HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                    VerticalContentAlignment="Center" />
        </StackPanel>
    </Grid>
</Window>
